<title>UK: Brazil prices $750 million five-year global bond.</title>
<headline>Brazil prices $750 million five-year global bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following global bond has been priced, joint lead managers J.P. Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg said on Monday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BRAZIL</p>
<p> AMT	  $750 MLN  COUPON     8.875     MATURITY    05.NOV.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.857    PAY DATE    05.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.50	REOFFER    99.857    SPREAD	+265 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B+	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  B-	  DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS UK/BR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  BRAZIL    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 31.OCT.01 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
